#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""A conversation's changes for the review view, and review feedback typed into its tmux pane.

Usage:
  ai-todo-review status <cwd> [--ref <branch>]
  ai-todo-review diff <cwd> [--scope uncommitted|branch|since] [--from <sha>] [--to <sha>]
                            [--unified N] [--max-bytes N] [--ref <branch>]
  ai-todo-review keep <cwd> <sha>
  ai-todo-review log <cwd> [--limit N] [--before <ISO time>] [--ref <branch>]
  ai-todo-review send [--base64] <tmux_name>   (the message on stdin)
  ai-todo-review run <cwd> --from <sha> --to <sha> --tool claude|codex --id <id> [--ref <branch>]
                         [--model M] [--context <path>]... [--brief-base64]   (the brief on stdin)
  ai-todo-review result <id>
  ai-todo-review cancel <id>
  ai-todo-review pr <cwd> [--ref <branch>] [--number N]
  ai-todo-review threads <cwd> [--ref <branch>] [--number N]
  ai-todo-review publish <cwd> --number N --head <sha>   (the review, base64 JSON, on stdin)
  ai-todo-review worktrees <cwd> [--since <ISO time>]
  ai-todo-review prs <cwd> [--since <ISO time>]
  ai-todo-review fetch-pr <cwd> --number N
  ai-todo-review merge <cwd> --number N --head <sha> --method merge|squash|rebase [--delete-branch]

Every command but send prints JSON.

A revision is a commit sha. With nothing uncommitted it is HEAD. Otherwise it is a snapshot
commit on top of HEAD, made from a temporary index (`git add -A`), so untracked files are in
it and neither the real index, the working tree nor the stash stack is touched. The snapshot
has a fixed author, committer, date and message, so the same worktree gives the same sha.

status  root, branch, head, upstream with ahead/behind, the branch's base (merge-base with
        origin's default branch) and the current revision. worktree_base: when the repository
        is a worktree the runner or app made (runner-state/worktrees.json), the commit it was
        made from (its merge-base with HEAD, so a branch kept from an earlier worktree counts
        from where it began); else null.
--ref   reviews that branch of the repository instead of its working tree: HEAD is the
        branch's tip, the revision is that commit and nothing is uncommitted. For a
        conversation whose worktree is gone but whose branch is kept in the project folder.
diff    a unified diff of the repository (paths from its root) from --from to --to (default:
        the current revision). --scope picks --from: uncommitted = HEAD (default), branch = the
        base, since = --from as given. --unified 0 is for moving comments between revisions.
keep    refs/ai-review/<sha> -> sha, so a revision feedback was sent against survives gc.
log     HEAD's recent commits (first parent): sha, subject, committer date, and whether the
        upstream has it (null without an upstream). --before: also the last commit made before
        that time ("before"), the start of a conversation that began then; null when none was.
send    pastes stdin into the tmux session `<tmux_name>` as a bracketed paste, then Return.
        --base64: stdin is base64 (the app sends it so; decoding here needs no base64 flags).
        Paste end markers (ESC[201~) in the message are dropped, so it can't end the paste
        early. Refused (exit 75) while the program there hasn't turned bracketed paste on:
        line by line, every newline would submit.

run     starts a reviewer agent on the changes --from..--to, detached, and prints {"id", "state"}
        at once. claude runs as `claude -p` with only Read, Grep and Glob; codex as `codex exec`
        in its read-only sandbox. It reads the files as of --to, exported into the run's folder
        (the working tree may change while it reads). Context goes in
        as paths it may read: the brief (the todo's title and notes, base64 on stdin with
        --brief-base64), AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md (the root's and those above changed files),
        docs/adr and spec folders, and every --context path. The run's files are in
        ~/.ai-remote/review-runs/<id> (AI_TODO_REVIEW_RUNS_DIR); runs older than 7 days go.
result  {"id", "state": running|done|failed|cancelled, "error", "result"}. A done run's result:
        tool, model, from, to, summary, usage (tokens and cost when the tool reports them, else
        null) and findings: path, side (new|old), line_start, line_end (null for the whole
        file), severity (high|medium|low), category, title, body, quote (the lines, from git,
        not the model) and fingerprint (path + title + nearby code, not line numbers, so the
        same finding on moved lines matches).
pr      the pull/merge request of the branch (GitHub with gh, GitLab with glab, by origin's URL or
        `git config ai-remote.forge`): {provider, access, error, viewer (who gh/glab act as),
        branch, pr}. pr: number, url, title, body, state (open|merged|closed), draft, author,
        review_decision, approvals, mergeable, checks {state passing|failing|pending|none, counts},
        head_sha, head_ref, base_ref; null when the branch has none. access false with error
        when the CLI is missing, logged out or failing: nothing else depends on it. Read-only.
threads its review threads on lines: {provider, access, error, pr, threads: [{id, path, side,
        line_start, line_end, commit, resolved, outdated, url, comments [{author, body,
        created_at}]}]}. GitHub: GraphQL reviewThreads; GitLab: the MR's discussions. The lines
        are in `commit`: the head (base for removed lines), or for an outdated GitHub thread
        the commit it was written on. --number with --url (GitHub) or --project (GitLab), as
        `pr` printed them, skips looking the PR up again.
publish posts a review on the PR/MR, as the computer's gh/glab account: {event COMMENT|APPROVE|
        REQUEST_CHANGES, body, comments [{path, side, line_start, line_end, body}]}, lines of
        --head. GitHub: one review against commit_id = --head, all or nothing. GitLab: one
        discussion per comment on the MR's diff refs (the user's own drafts stay drafts), the
        summary as a note, then approve with sha. Exit 67 when the head isn't --head any more.
merge   merges it through the API (nothing changes in the worktree) only while its head is
        --head, deleting the branch on the forge when asked. GitLab must answer merged: queued
        for a pipeline is a failure. Branch protection and checks are the forge's to enforce.
prs     the PRs/MRs the computer's gh/glab account opened in origin, newest first, marking those
        updated since --since. fetch-pr: one's head into refs/ai-review/pr/N and its base
        branch; prints head and the merge base, so `diff --scope since --from base --to head`
        is exactly its changes.
worktrees  the repository's worktrees (not a bare one), most recently active first (last commit or
        HEAD move), marking those active since
        --since: for an agent that made its own worktree outside the conversation's folder.
cancel  stops a running reviewer (its whole process group). Prints what `result` does: a run
        that finished first stays done, with its findings.

Exit codes: 64 bad arguments, 65 unknown revision or empty message (or nothing to publish),
67 the PR/MR moved on from --head, 77 gh/glab failed (their words on stderr), 78 some
GitLab comments were posted before a later step failed, 66 no such tmux
session, 69 not a git repository (or cwd missing), 70 git failed (its message on stderr),
75 the pane isn't ready for a paste, 90 git, tmux, claude or codex missing.
"""
import base64
import binascii
import calendar
import glob
import hashlib
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import time

HOME = os.path.expanduser("~")

SNAPSHOT_IDENT = {
    "GIT_AUTHOR_NAME": "ai-review", "GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL": "ai-review@localhost",
    "GIT_COMMITTER_NAME": "ai-review", "GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL": "ai-review@localhost",
    "GIT_AUTHOR_DATE": "@0 +0000", "GIT_COMMITTER_DATE": "@0 +0000",
}
SNAPSHOT_MESSAGE = "ai-review snapshot\n"
KEEP_PREFIX = "refs/ai-review/"
DEFAULT_MAX_BYTES = 4 * 1024 * 1024
# The user's git config must not change what is parsed: no colour, prefixes, external diffs.
DIFF_CONFIG = ["-c", "diff.noprefix=false", "-c", "diff.mnemonicPrefix=false",
               "-c", "diff.external=", "-c", "color.ui=never", "-c", "core.quotePath=false"]


def die(message, code):
    sys.stderr.write("ai-todo-review: %s\n" % message)
    sys.exit(code)


def die_missing(program):
    """Exit 90 with a bare `<program> not found`, the line the app reads the name from."""
    sys.stderr.write("%s not found\n" % program)
    sys.exit(90)


def git(cwd, *args, env=None, check=True, text=True):
    full_env = dict(os.environ)
    full_env.pop("GIT_DIR", None)
    full_env.pop("GIT_WORK_TREE", None)
    full_env.pop("GIT_INDEX_FILE", None)
    full_env["GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS"] = "0"
    if env:
        full_env.update(env)
    try:
        result = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", cwd] + list(args), stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
                                stderr=subprocess.PIPE, env=full_env)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        die_missing("git")
    if check and result.returncode != 0:
        raise GitError(result.stderr.decode("utf-8", "replace").strip())
    out = result.stdout
    return (out.decode("utf-8", "replace") if text else out), result.returncode


class GitError(Exception):
    pass


def line(cwd, *args):
    """First line of output, or None when the command fails."""
    try:
        out, _ = git(cwd, *args)
    except GitError:
        return None
    out = out.strip()
    return out.splitlines()[0] if out else None


def repo_root(cwd):
    path = os.path.expanduser(cwd)
    if not os.path.isdir(path):
        die("no folder %s" % cwd, 69)
    root = line(path, "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel")
    if not root:
        die("%s is not in a git repository" % cwd, 69)
    return root


def head_sha(root):
    return line(root, "rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", "HEAD^{commit}")


def snapshot(root):
    """(revision sha, clean). Built in a temporary index. The snapshot index of the last call
    (this worktree's `ai-review-index`, else the real index) seeds it, so files whose stat data
    didn't change, untracked ones included, aren't hashed again. Calls at the same time each
    work on their own copy; the last one to finish leaves its index for the next."""
    head = head_sha(root)
    index = line(root, "rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-path", "index")
    kept = line(root, "rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-path", "ai-review-index")
    tmpdir = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="ai-review-", dir=os.path.dirname(kept) if kept else None)
    try:
        tmp_index = os.path.join(tmpdir, "index")
        seed = kept if kept and os.path.exists(kept) else index
        if seed and os.path.exists(seed):
            # copy2 keeps the mtime: git re-checks entries as new as the index (racy-git)
            shutil.copy2(seed, tmp_index)
        env = {"GIT_INDEX_FILE": tmp_index}
        git(root, "add", "-A", "--", ".", env=env)
        tree, _ = git(root, "write-tree", env=env)
        tree = tree.strip()
        if kept:
            try:
                os.replace(tmp_index, kept)
            except OSError:
                pass
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(tmpdir, ignore_errors=True)
    if head and line(root, "rev-parse", head + "^{tree}") == tree:
        return head, True
    args = ["commit-tree", tree, "-m", SNAPSHOT_MESSAGE.strip()]
    if head:
        args[2:2] = ["-p", head]
    env = dict(SNAPSHOT_IDENT)
    sha, _ = git(root, *args, env=env)
    return sha.strip(), False


def default_branch_ref(root):
    ref = line(root, "symbolic-ref", "-q", "refs/remotes/origin/HEAD")
    candidates = ([ref] if ref else []) + ["refs/remotes/origin/main", "refs/remotes/origin/master",
                                           "refs/heads/main", "refs/heads/master"]
    for candidate in candidates:
        if line(root, "rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", candidate):
            return candidate
    return None


def short_ref(ref):
    for prefix in ("refs/remotes/", "refs/heads/"):
        if ref.startswith(prefix):
            return ref[len(prefix):]
    return ref


def base_of(root, head):
    ref = default_branch_ref(root)
    if not ref or not head:
        return None
    sha = line(root, "merge-base", head, ref)
    return {"ref": short_ref(ref), "sha": sha} if sha else None


def registry_file():
    state = os.environ.get("AI_TODO_RUNNER_STATE_DIR") or os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), ".ai-remote", "runner-state")
    return os.path.join(state, "worktrees.json")


def worktree_base(root, head):
    """The commit this worktree was made from, when the runner or app made it; else None."""
    try:
        with open(registry_file()) as handle:
            registry = json.load(handle)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    entries = registry.values() if isinstance(registry, dict) else registry if isinstance(registry, list) else []
    real = os.path.realpath(root)
    for entry in entries:
        if not isinstance(entry, dict) or not entry.get("base") or not entry.get("path"):
            continue
        if os.path.realpath(entry["path"]) != real:
            continue
        base = line(root, "rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", entry["base"] + "^{commit}")
        if not base:
            return None
        return (line(root, "merge-base", base, head) if head else None) or base
    return None


def ref_sha(root, ref):
    """The tip of branch `ref` (or `origin/<branch>`: a pushed branch with no local copy), or
    exit 65 when the repository has no such branch."""
    sha = line(root, "rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", "refs/heads/%s^{commit}" % ref)
    if not sha and ref.startswith("origin/"):
        sha = line(root, "rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", "refs/remotes/%s^{commit}" % ref)
    if not sha:
        die("no branch %s" % ref, 65)
    return sha


def take_ref(args):
    """(args without `--ref X`, X or None)."""
    rest = list(args)
    if "--ref" not in rest:
        return rest, None
    at = rest.index("--ref")
    if at + 1 >= len(rest) or not rest[at + 1] or rest[at + 1].startswith("-"):
        die("--ref needs a branch", 64)
    ref = rest[at + 1]
    del rest[at:at + 2]
    return rest, ref


def cmd_status(args):
    args, ref = take_ref(args)
    if len(args) != 1:
        die("usage: ai-todo-review status <cwd> [--ref <branch>]", 64)
    root = repo_root(args[0])
    if ref:
        head = ref_sha(root, ref)
        branch = ref
        upstream = line(root, "rev-parse", "--abbrev-ref", "--symbolic-full-name", "refs/heads/%s@{upstream}" % ref)
    else:
        head = head_sha(root)
        branch = line(root, "symbolic-ref", "-q", "--short", "HEAD")
        upstream = line(root, "rev-parse", "--abbrev-ref", "--symbolic-full-name", "@{upstream}")
    ahead = behind = None
    if upstream and head:
        counts = line(root, "rev-list", "--left-right", "--count", "%s...%s" % (head, upstream))
        if counts and len(counts.split()) == 2:
            ahead, behind = (int(n) for n in counts.split())
    revision, clean = (head, True) if ref else snapshot(root)
    print(json.dumps({
        "root": root,
        "branch": branch,
        "head": head,
        "upstream": upstream,
        "ahead": ahead,
        "behind": behind,
        "base": base_of(root, head),
        "revision": revision,
        "clean": clean,
        "worktree_base": None if ref else worktree_base(root, head),
        "ref": ref,
    }))


def cmd_diff(args):
    args, ref = take_ref(args)
    cwd = None
    scope = "uncommitted"
    from_sha = to_sha = None
    unified = 3
    max_bytes = DEFAULT_MAX_BYTES
    rest = list(args)
    try:
        while rest:
            arg = rest.pop(0)
            if arg == "--scope":
                scope = rest.pop(0)
            elif arg == "--from":
                from_sha = rest.pop(0)
            elif arg == "--to":
                to_sha = rest.pop(0)
            elif arg == "--unified":
                unified = int(rest.pop(0))
            elif arg == "--max-bytes":
                max_bytes = int(rest.pop(0))
            elif arg.startswith("-") or cwd is not None:
                raise ValueError(arg)
            else:
                cwd = arg
    except (IndexError, ValueError):
        die("usage: ai-todo-review diff <cwd> [--scope uncommitted|branch|since] [--from <sha>] "
            "[--to <sha>] [--unified N] [--max-bytes N]", 64)
    if cwd is None or scope not in ("uncommitted", "branch", "since") or unified < 0 or max_bytes < 1:
        die("usage: ai-todo-review diff <cwd> [--scope uncommitted|branch|since] ...", 64)
    root = repo_root(cwd)
    head = ref_sha(root, ref) if ref else head_sha(root)
    if to_sha is None:
        to_sha = head if ref else snapshot(root)[0]
    if scope == "since":
        if not from_sha:
            die("--scope since needs --from <sha>", 64)
    elif scope == "branch":
        base = base_of(root, head)
        from_sha = base["sha"] if base else head
    elif from_sha is None:
        from_sha = head
    for sha in (from_sha, to_sha):
        if sha and not line(root, "rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", sha + "^{commit}"):
            die("unknown revision %s" % sha, 65)
    if from_sha is None:
        # No commits yet: everything is new.
        from_sha = line(root, "hash-object", "-t", "tree", "/dev/null")
    # Explicit prefixes: diff.srcPrefix / diff.dstPrefix (git 2.45+) would change them.
    patch, _ = git(root, *DIFF_CONFIG, "diff", "--no-color", "--no-ext-diff", "--no-textconv",
                   "--src-prefix=a/", "--dst-prefix=b/", "-M", "--unified=%d" % unified, from_sha, to_sha, "--", text=False)
    truncated = len(patch) > max_bytes
    if truncated:
        cut = patch.rfind(b"\ndiff --git ", 0, max_bytes)
        # Whole files only: a file cut mid-hunk would move comments as if its tail were unchanged.
        patch = patch[:cut + 1] if cut > 0 else b""
    print(json.dumps({
        "from": from_sha,
        "to": to_sha,
        "scope": scope,
        "patch": patch.decode("utf-8", "replace"),
        "truncated": truncated,
    }))


def cmd_log(args):
    args, ref = take_ref(args)
    limit = 30
    before = None
    rest = list(args)
    cwd = None
    try:
        while rest:
            arg = rest.pop(0)
            if arg == "--limit":
                limit = int(rest.pop(0))
            elif arg == "--before":
                before = rest.pop(0)
            elif arg.startswith("-") or cwd is not None:
                raise ValueError(arg)
            else:
                cwd = arg
    except (IndexError, ValueError):
        cwd = None
    if cwd is None or not 1 <= limit <= 500 or (before is not None and not before.strip()):
        die("usage: ai-todo-review log <cwd> [--limit N] [--before <ISO time>]", 64)
    root = repo_root(cwd)
    head = ref_sha(root, ref) if ref else head_sha(root)
    commits = []
    found_before = None
    if head:
        out, _ = git(root, "log", "--first-parent", "-n", str(limit), "--format=%H%x1f%s%x1f%cI", head)
        unpushed = None
        upstream = line(root, "rev-parse", "--abbrev-ref", "--symbolic-full-name",
                        ("refs/heads/%s@{upstream}" % ref) if ref else "@{upstream}")
        if upstream:
            listed, _ = git(root, "rev-list", "%s..%s" % (upstream, head))
            unpushed = set(listed.split())
        for row in out.splitlines():
            parts = row.split("\x1f")
            if len(parts) != 3:
                continue
            sha, subject, date = parts
            commits.append({"sha": sha, "subject": subject, "date": date,
                            "pushed": None if unpushed is None else sha not in unpushed})
        if before is not None:
            found_before = line(root, "rev-list", "--first-parent", "-n", "1", "--before=" + before, head)
    print(json.dumps({"commits": commits, "before": found_before}))


def cmd_keep(args):
    if len(args) != 2:
        die("usage: ai-todo-review keep <cwd> <sha>", 64)
    root = repo_root(args[0])
    sha = line(root, "rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", args[1] + "^{commit}")
    if not sha:
        die("unknown revision %s" % args[1], 65)
    git(root, "update-ref", KEEP_PREFIX + sha, sha)
    print(json.dumps({"kept": sha}))


def tmux(*args, stdin=None):
    socket = os.environ.get("AI_TODO_TMUX_SOCKET")
    command = ["tmux"] + (["-L", socket] if socket else []) + list(args)
    try:
        return subprocess.run(command, input=stdin, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        die_missing("tmux")


PASTE_END = b"\x1b[201~"
PASTE_SETTLE_SECONDS = float(os.environ.get("AI_TODO_REVIEW_PASTE_SETTLE", "0.3"))


def cmd_send(args):
    encoded = bool(args) and args[0] == "--base64"
    if encoded:
        args = args[1:]
    if len(args) != 1 or not args[0]:
        die("usage: ai-todo-review send [--base64] <tmux_name> < message", 64)
    name = args[0]
    message = sys.stdin.buffer.read()
    if encoded:
        try:
            message = base64.b64decode(message.strip(), validate=True)
        except (binascii.Error, ValueError):
            die("the message isn't base64", 64)
    # Removing one marker can join the pieces around it into another.
    while PASTE_END in message:
        message = message.replace(PASTE_END, b"")
    if not message.strip():
        die("empty message", 65)
    if tmux("has-session", "-t", "=" + name).returncode != 0:
        die("no tmux session %s" % name, 66)
    # The tool runs in the session's first pane (ai-todo-open starts it there). Not the active
    # one: a shell opened beside it would run the feedback as commands.
    panes = tmux("list-panes", "-s", "-t", "=" + name, "-F", "#{window_index} #{pane_index} #{pane_id}")
    rows = []
    for row in panes.stdout.decode().splitlines():
        parts = row.split()
        if len(parts) == 3 and parts[0].isdigit() and parts[1].isdigit():
            rows.append((int(parts[0]), int(parts[1]), parts[2]))
    if panes.returncode != 0 or not rows:
        die("no pane in %s" % name, 66)
    target = min(rows)[2]
    # "1": the program turned bracketed paste on. Empty: a tmux without this format (unknown),
    # where the agent, once running, has it on.
    flag = tmux("display-message", "-p", "-t", target, "#{bracket_paste_flag}")
    if flag.returncode != 0 or flag.stdout.decode().strip() not in ("1", ""):
        die("%s isn't ready for a paste" % name, 75)
    buffer = "ai-review-%d" % os.getpid()
    if tmux("load-buffer", "-b", buffer, "-", stdin=message.rstrip(b"\n")).returncode != 0:
        die("couldn't load the message into tmux", 75)
    pasted = tmux("paste-buffer", "-p", "-d", "-b", buffer, "-t", target)
    if pasted.returncode != 0:
        tmux("delete-buffer", "-b", buffer)
        die("couldn't paste into %s" % name, 75)
    # A TUI may still be taking in a long paste; Return inside that would only add a line.
    time.sleep(PASTE_SETTLE_SECONDS)
    tmux("send-keys", "-t", target, "Enter")
    print(json.dumps({"sent": len(message)}))


